/* ================================================================
   skin-skin1.css — "the handwritten wrapped in the computer"
   Built from Skin Explorations.dc.html: wrapper = system phosphor
   (Calibri/Carlito, aged yellow-green, glow only on headers);
   Blackboard = one wood-framed slate (Gaegu chalk, dark slate);
   Inventory = kraft tag-cards (Special Elite + Caveat, paper).
   Drop into /static/skin-skin1.css and load the board with
   ?skin=skin1. See SKIN-SPEC.md for the decisions behind this file.
   ================================================================ */

//
// Each public function takes (node, lens) and returns ONE visual value per CONTRACTS.md.
// No DOM, no three.js, no side effects on import. Data in, value out.
//
// CONTRACT 1 (NODE): nodes carry raw attrs (status/type/energy/… possibly null) plus a
//   normalized block `node.n` where every quantitative field is 0..1 (or null if the raw
//   value was absent). We read `node.n.<field>` for sizing/y, raw attrs for hue/shape/highlight.
// CONTRACT 2 (LENS): lens.hueBy / shapeBy / sizeBy / yMode / highlight / score select the mapping.
//
// EXTENSION POINTS are marked `// EXTEND:` — add a case to the relevant switch to grow a lever.

// ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
// PALETTE — exported so panel/legend can reuse the exact same colors.
//   status: the FROZEN status hex map (do not change these values).
//   domain/type: two DISTINCT 6-hex categorical scales.
//   NULL: the fallback for any absent categorical value.
// ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

// ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
// colorFor(node, lens) → "#rrggbb"
//   by lens.hueBy. Null categorical value → PALETTE.NULL.

// ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
// shapeFor(node, lens) → geometry name
//   by lens.shapeBy. "none" → sphere. Null categorical → sphere.

// ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
// yFor(node, lens) → number|null   (0..1 target height, or null when axis is free)
//   "free" → null (let the simulation place y).
//   "recency" → 1 - n.recency  (stale = high recency value = sinks low).
//   "age"     → 1 - n.age      (old = high age value = sinks low).
//   "score"   → scoreFor       (high score rises).
//   Null metric → 0.5 (neutral mid-plane).

// ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
// matchesHighlight(node, lens) → boolean
//   "active"→status active · "urgent"→urgent · "important"→important
//   "energyHi"→energy hi · "none"→false.

// ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
// __selftest() — runs the mappings over mock nodes + lenses and logs outputs.
//   NOTE: score.js may not exist in this session; scoreFor is imported per contract
//   but the score-dependent cases are exercised defensively (a thrown import would
//   surface at module load, which the assembly step resolves).

